# Visual Design Update for Horace Englossed Interactive Digital Edition

## Introduction
This document summarizes the actual visual and UI design of the Horace Englossed digital edition to date, reflecting implemented features and current layout, as well as commenting on design evolution.

## Realized Color Scheme
- **Primary Accent**: Warm Beige/Cream (#faf8f4, #fcf8f2, #f9f6eb)
- **Supporting Neutrals**: Pale brown and light tan (#e7dec7, #ede5cd, #f5f0e9)
- **Text Color**: Muted brown to deep charcoal (#4A2C2C, #365257)
- **Highlight**: Light yellow for glosses (#fff9c4), blue for metamarks (#bbdefb)
- **Secondary Accent (Buttons, Links)**: Deep brown (#4a2c2c), Gold/bronze (#D4A574 for hovers/accents)
- **Footer/Impressum**: Faint gray-brown, small font for subtlety (#998678, #b6a799)

### Tablet/Mobile View
- **Headings and buttons stack, split switches to vertical (columns to full-width rows)**
- Poem appears first, toggles above or below, then the TEI or manuscript images as one column below.
- All elements remain readable and scrollable.

## Typography
- **Headings**: Serif font ('Garamond' or 'Playfair Display'), large, centered
- **Body Text**: Georgia/serif, comfortable for scholarly reading
- **Buttons**: Sans-serif for clarity; bold, bronze highlight on hover
- **Glosses/Metamarks**: Italic/colored, background highlight, dashed border
- **Footer/Impressum**: Smaller font, faint color, centered
